# Enpal Patterns

## Architecture

- `main.js` — adapter class (`Enpal extends utils.Adapter`): Influx polling, CSV parsing, state creation, optional wallbox control
- `lib/wallbox.js` — Blazor SignalR client for Enpal Box `/wallbox` page (wallbox control only)
- Data sources:
  - **Read:** local InfluxDB 2.x (Enpal system), polled via HTTP/HTTPS
  - **Control (optional):** Enpal Box web interface via Blazor WebSocket

## InfluxDB connection

- Query API: `POST /api/v2/query?org=<org>`
- Headers:
  - `Authorization: Token <token>`
  - `Content-Type: application/vnd.flux`
  - `Accept: application/csv`
- Protocol: use `node:http` or `node:https` based on configured URL (`queryInflux()`)
- On HTTP errors: set `info.connection` to `false` and log clearly
- **Avoid:** axios, request, or other HTTP libraries

## Polling and lifecycle

- Interval: `native.interval_s` (seconds, default 60)
- Start polling with `this.setInterval` in `onReady()`; stop with `this.clearInterval` in `onUnload()`
- In `onReady()`: set `info.connection` to `false` first; switch to `true` only after a successful query
- Always call `callback()` in `onUnload()`, even on error

## State model (InfluxDB)

- States are created dynamically from Influx CSV rows
- Full ID schema: `enpal.<instance>.<measurement>.<device>.<field>`
- Without device tag: `enpal.<instance>.<measurement>.<field>`
- Sanitize: characters outside `[a-zA-Z0-9_-]` → `_`
- Units: `Percent` → `%`; `None` → empty unit (not displayed)

## State model (Wallbox control)

- Fixed channel `wallbox_control` — created only when `wallbox_enabled` is true
- States:
  - `wallbox_control.start` — boolean button (write `true` to start charging)
  - `wallbox_control.stop` — boolean button (write `true` to stop charging)
  - `wallbox_control.mode` — string enum: `eco`, `solar`, `full`, `smart`
  - `wallbox_control.currentMode` — read-only, synced from Enpal Box HTML
  - `wallbox_control.connectorStatus` — read-only, synced from Enpal Box HTML
- Wallbox status is refreshed on each Influx poll cycle via HTTP GET `/wallbox`
- WebSocket connection is opened on demand for control commands (not kept permanently)

## Wallbox control (lib/wallbox.js)

- Requires Enpal firmware 8.50+ with `/wallbox` Blazor page
- Flow: GET `/wallbox` → negotiate `/_blazor` → WebSocket → StartCircuit → parse RenderBatch for button handler IDs → click via `BeginInvokeDotNetFromJS`
- Reference implementation: [derolli1976/enpal](https://github.com/derolli1976/enpal) (`api/wallbox_client.py`)
- No external npm dependencies — MessagePack encoder/decoder is inline

## Key functions

### main.js

- `queryInflux()` — protocol-aware HTTP request to InfluxDB
- `parseCsv()` — must stay robust against incomplete/commented CSV lines
- `ensureParentChannels()` — creates missing channel hierarchy before state creation
- `syncInfluxToIoBroker()` — central sync path; must not crash on errors
- `_initWallbox()` / `_createWallboxStates()` / `_syncWallboxStatus()` / `onStateChange()` — wallbox control

### lib/wallbox.js

- `WallboxBlazorClient` — connect, clickButton, start/stop/setMode, fetchStatus
- `extractStatusFromHtml()` — parse mode/status from pre-rendered `/wallbox` HTML

## Pitfalls

- Do not change Influx datapoint naming or parsing without considering backward compatibility
- Do not retry failed Influx queries in a tight loop — wait for the next poll cycle
- `syncInfluxToIoBroker()` returns early on query failure or empty results (connection stays `false`)
- Wallbox control is reverse-engineered — Enpal firmware updates may break the Blazor protocol
- Avoid parallel wallbox control from multiple clients (GUI, HA, ioBroker) at the same time
